    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s ally Louis X became Grand Duke Louis I in 1806 and later exchanged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westphalia">Westphalia</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhenish-hesse">Rhenish Hesse</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a>.</li><li>Its constitution of 1820 joined Lutheran <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/starkenburg">Starkenburg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-hesse">Upper Hesse</a> with Catholic, French-law <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhenish-hesse">Rhenish Hesse</a>.</li><li>Defeated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> in 1866, it joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> in 1871 and ended with the deposition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ernest-louis-grand-duke-of-hesse">Ernest Louis</a> in 1918.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>After 1866 the grand duchy was split: its province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-hesse">Upper Hesse</a> had to join the North German Confederation, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/starkenburg">Starkenburg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhenish-hesse">Rhenish Hesse</a> stayed outside until 1871.</p></aside>
    </section>

